\title{DAG #{\to} indegree 0}
\date{2026-09-24T15:50:16Z}
\tag{algorithms}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\taxon{Lemma}
\p{Any [DAG](00N9) has a vertex with [indegree](00N7) #{0}.}

\proof{
Pick any starting vertex #{v}, and keep following incoming edges backwards until finding a vertex with no incoming edges. This process must stop: if not, by the pigeonhole principle, since there are only finitely many vertices, we must eventually visit a vertex twice, but this would form a directed cycle, and we assumed the graph is a DAG.
}

\transclude{00NF}   % infinite DAGs?
